InternetDJ's favorite House master Roger Sanchez will be spinning at the World, NYC. <br><br><b>Who:</b> <br> As one of the planet’s foremost house DJs, Roger Sanchez has the art of making people feel right down to an exact science. <br> <br> <b>What:</b> <br> From low-key residencies in his native New York to the wide open spaces of Ibiza or London’s Fabric, Roger Sanchez has taken his distinctively soulful, experimental sets around the world. His skills of DJing hip-hop to house music with a third turntable and masterly scratching techniques distinguish him as an infamous pro. <br> <br> <b>Where:</b> <br> The World @ 43rd Street and Broadway <br> (Entrance is located on 43rd Street) <br> <br> <b>When:</b> <br> Saturday, February 23, 2002 <br> Doors open 11:00 p.m. <br> <br> <b>Why:</b> <br> Because NYC’s in a bump-and-grind frenzy! <br> <br> <b>How:</b> <br> Tickets available day of event at: <br> The World @ 43rd Street and Broadway, Times Square, 212-398-3439 <br> <br> Price of General Admission $30.00. <br> <br> Must be 18 to enter, 21 and over to drink. <br> Proper I.D. required. Proper attire required. <br> <br> For more information on ticket purchases and events call: <br> 212-398-2563 or visit www.TheWorldNY.com. <br> &nbsp; <img src="themes/internetdj/images/header_extras.gif"> <br>&nbsp;<a href="search.php?topic=32"><b>More DJ News</b></a><br> <br><hr noshade size="1"> <b>Most read story in DJ News:</b><br>
