BBC's Radio 1 is throwing a contest where you can work on an original club track with the legendary DJ and Producer Rui Da Silva. These are the details you're looking for. <br><br>Here's the take from BBC's Radio 1: Is it your dream to work on a house track with a number one-selling artist? Well this is an amazing, money-can’t-buy, opportunity for you. We’re giving you the chance to win studio time with the DJ and Producer, Rui Da Silva. <br /> <br /> He was of course the man behind the massive number 1 single, “Touch Me” and he’s inviting you to help him record a track for his forthcoming album. How cool is that? So if you fancy working with a true professional and have loads of ideas, then this could be a fantastic opportunity for you. <br /> <br /> We’re obviously looking for someone who’s really interested in making house music, and would make a valuable contribution to the session. So, to prove you are talented and have what it takes, we would like to hear what you’re made of! <br /> <br /> We want to hear any relevant demos that you may have made to judge whether you would be a good studio partner for Rui. And remember it’s not necessarily about the quality of the demo, it’s about the quality of the ideas. <br /> <br /> Send your entries to: <br /> <br /> RUI DA SILVA COMPETITION<br /> DANCE ANTHEMS <br /> BBC RADIO 1<br /> LONDON<br /> W1N 4DJ<br /> <br /> But get them in quick, as the deadline is 29th January!! Runners up will also win themselves Kismet backcatalogue - that’s the label Rui’s records for... <br><br> <b>Other Links</b><br> · <a href="http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/redirect?tag=theinternedj&creative=9353&camp=1793&link_code=st1&path=ASIN/B00005AWUI">Rui Da Silva @ Amazon</a> <br> &nbsp; &nbsp; Extras <br>&nbsp;<a href="search.php?topic=32"><b>More DJ News</b></a><br> <br><hr noshade size="1"> <b>Most read story in DJ News:</b><br>
